  "chapter": 698,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 44 Chapter 698\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 1684-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the emergency tenant protection act of nineteen\n        seventy-four, in relation to studies to determine vacancy rates\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require rental housing owners to  reply  to  municipal\nsurveys  to  determine whether the rental vacancy rate is low enough for\nthe municipality to enter rent stabilization under the Emergency  Tenant\nProtection  Act  (ETPA).  The  bill would allow municipalities to impose\nseveral penalties upon owners who refuse to participate in the survey or\nsubmit knowingly and intentionally false information.\n \n  I support the goals of this legislation, which would increase  compli-\nance  with  municipal vacancy rate surveys and shed much-needed light on\nthe housing market in communities  across  New  York.  However,  certain\nchanges  were  necessary to ensure any penalties levied are commensurate\nto the misconduct of rental housing  owners  while  also  ensuring  that\nlevying  penalties  on bad actors does not unintentionally lead to fewer\nrental units being offered on the market. These changes include removing\ncertain administrative  penalties  and  setting  the  maximum  financial\npenalty to $500.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
